{
  "source": "Build a character animation called Matrix rain.\nUse the standard character canvas and a complete repeating sequence.\nShow green characters on a black background with the brightest leading characters and progressively darker trails.\n\nAsk the model to make letters.\nChoose the uppercase English letter at the requested position and repeat the alphabet after its end.\nUse no earlier steps.\nCheck the beginning, the end and repeated journeys through the alphabet.\nFinish this step.\n\nAsk the model to make movement.\nMove a row by the requested distance and wrap between the bottom and the top in either direction.\nUse no earlier steps.\nCheck every canvas row with forward, backward and stationary movement.\nFinish this step.\n\nAsk the model to make leading positions.\nStart the leftmost column at the top.\nStart each following column below the previous column by the trail length and wrap below the bottom to the top.\nMove the leftmost column downward at normal speed.\nAlternate each following column between double speed and normal speed.\nUse only movement.\nCheck the initial positions, both speeds and repeated journeys through the canvas.\nFinish this step.\n\nAsk the model to make trailing positions.\nPlace each later trail character immediately above the previous character and wrap above the top to the bottom.\nUse only movement.\nCheck every trail position at the top, middle and bottom of the canvas.\nFinish this step.\n\nAsk the model to make shades.\nGive the leading character the brightest shade and make each later trail character progressively darker until the darkest shade.\nUse no earlier steps.\nCheck the leading shade, every trail shade and saturation at the darkest shade.\nFinish this step.\n\nAsk the model to make frames.\nFill each separate vertical column with its leading character and trailing characters.\nChoose each character from its column position plus the elapsed frame position plus its distance behind the leader.\nRestart the frame position at the beginning whenever the complete canvas cycle finishes.\nUse the restarted frame position for both character selection and movement so that every repetition begins identically.\nUse only letters and leading positions and trailing positions and shades.\nCheck every character position, letter and shade against the earlier accepted steps.\nFinish this step.\n\nAsk the model to make animation.\nCreate successive frames from the initial canvas until every stream returns to its starting position.\nUse only frames.\nCheck the complete sequence, its ordering and its return to the initial frame.\nFinish this step.\n\nDisplay the accepted animation and repeat it in the character player.\n",
